# Plaintext content backups — must never be committed, they would
# re-expose premium content that is encrypted everywhere else.
data/Orals/Backup/
data/**/Backup/
data/PLAINTEXT_BACKUP_do_not_delete/
# Root-level backups too. The rule above only matches a Backup/ nested under
# data/, so top-level ones fell straight through: Backup/ (278 plaintext Oral
# files, 9.1 MB) and _backup_Sandra/ (46 more), both of which `git add -A`
# staged in full. Neither was ever committed, caught first.
#
# A plaintext copy of paid content in a public repo defeats the encryption
# completely: a competitor gets the whole Oral course from one `git clone`,
# no account needed. That is the exact scenario the encryption was added to
# prevent, so match these wherever they sit, not just under data/.
/Backup/
/_backup_Sandra/
# Catch-all for future ones, since these keep appearing under new names.
# Verify with: git status --porcelain -uall | grep '^??'
/*backup*/
/*_bak/
/*.bak

# Local key storage — never commit real secret values
DecryptEncrypt/

# Supabase CLI local state, not project config
supabase/.temp/

# Tooling only (sharp, for diagram conversion). There is no package.json here;
# this repo ships as a static site, so node_modules is never part of a deploy.
node_modules/

# Local preview harness for the DI charts, not part of the site.
/_di_preview.html
/_di_preview_frame.html
# Build artifact from _digen.cjs
/_dicharts.json
/_di_pies.html
/_di_pies_frame.html
